{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-alpha-basis-knot-delta-q","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:alpha-basis-knot-delta-q","kind":"proposition","title":"q-dimension decoration of the basis knots: $\\delta_q(T_{2,k}) = h\\,[k]_q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio"],"tags":["alpha-basis-knot","q-dimension","quantum-integer","pre-archimedean","fine-structure-constant","hecke"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlphaBasisKnot.deltaQ_eq_h_qbracket","text":"alpha-basis-knot-delta-q.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-basis-knot-delta-q.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:alpha-basis-knot-delta-q\"></a><p><em>For the basis torus knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,k}</code>, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\delta_q</code>-decoration evaluates exactly as:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\delta_q(T_{2,k}) \\;=\\; q^{k} - q^{-k} \\;=\\; h\\,[k]_q.</code></pre>\n<p><em>The identity holds purely algebraically in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1/2}, h^{-1}]</code> with no archimedean approximation.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-basis-knot-delta-q.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.24.14"}
